---
description: C++ conventions, ownership, portability, and implementation practices.
globs: "**/*.h,**/*.hpp,**/*.cpp,**/*.cc"
alwaysApply: false
---
- Target C++20 for game code.
- Prefer RAII and deterministic lifetime.
- Prefer stack/value semantics. Use `std::unique_ptr` for dynamic ownership; avoid `std::shared_ptr` without a concrete ownership requirement.
- Use `std::filesystem` for paths.
- Treat asset path casing as case-sensitive on every platform.
- No OS-specific headers in gameplay files.
- No direct raylib calls from `game/source/gameplay/**`.
- Avoid per-frame heap allocation in hot paths.
- Keep public APIs small and explicit.
- Add assertions for programmer errors in Debug/Development where useful.
